{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When a man or woman shall clearly utter a vow.</b> יַפְרִישׁ — shall set apart. Why is the passage of the nazirite juxtaposed to the passage of the sotah? To tell you that anyone who sees a sotah in her corruption should become a nazirite, abstaining from wine — for wine brings to adultery (Sotah 2a)." "<b>The vow of a nazirite.</b> Naziriteship everywhere means abstention; so too here — he abstains from wine." "<b>To consecrate himself to YHWH.</b> To separate himself from wine for the sake of Heaven."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:44.264146726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}